if (result != ASN1_SUCCESS) {
    gnutls_assert();
    result = _gnutls_asn2err(result);
    goto cleanup;
}
```

If `asn1_read_value` fails, the function goes to cleanup. If it succeeds, `len` is updated. So `len` should always be updated on success.

